-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the abstract Hecke evaluation on S_k(Γ₀(N))
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$ and let $k$ be an integer. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) for the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ in one variable for each element of `Nat.Primes`, and let `heckeAlgebra N k ∅` be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_k(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$, the $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphisms of the space of cusp forms of weight $k$ for `CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N`, generated by the set `heckeGenerators N k ∅`. The map [`CuspForm.heckeEvalForms N k`](def/CuspForm_HeckeEvalForms.html#L26) is the ring homomorphism underlying the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra evaluation homomorphism $\mathbb{T} \to$ `heckeAlgebra N k ∅` that sends the variable indexed by a prime $\ell$ to `heckeFormsGen N k ℓ`, namely to the element `heckeAlgebra.U` at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and to the element `heckeAlgebra.T` at $\ell$ when $\ell \nmid N$ (the empty set playing the role of the excluded set of primes in both cases). The assertion is that the range of this ring homomorphism is the whole of `heckeAlgebra N k ∅`, i.e. that `heckeEvalForms N k` is surjective.
--
--   This records that the Hecke algebra acting on $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ is a quotient of the free abstract Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell]$, so that statements about modules over the abstract algebra transfer to the concrete one. It is used in the Hecke-module arguments on the modular curve side, for instance in the construction of Galois-equivariant families on Tate modules, in the production of Hecke idempotents attached to the Eisenstein part, and in the lattice computations that accompany them.
